WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.270
Showtime's horror drama Penny Dreadful dropped
its biggest twist during its season three

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:12.110
finale, "The Blessed Dark": the series was
over. While the show is still having its last

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:17.500
rites read, let's investigate the potentially
spoiler-filled mystery of why it had to end...

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.610
Declining viewership

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:23.200
The last season of Penny Dreadful was not
a ratings juggernaut, clocking in at number

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.899
six among Showtime’s ten original shows,
behind Billions and The Affair. Viewership

00:00:27.899 --> 00:00:32.410
had dropped over 5% compared to the previous
year. While other shows had fewer viewers,

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.239
Penny Dreadful’s elaborate settings and
special effects made it far more expensive

00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:40.399
to produce. A cult following just wasn't enough.
A little over half a million people watched

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:42.800
the series finale live.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:43.649
Money

00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:47.989
Like most TV cancellations, money was likely
a large factor in Showtime's decision to give

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:51.789
Penny Dreadful the axe. It happened to plenty
of other fan favorite shows over the years;

00:00:51.789 --> 00:00:56.769
Firefly, Hannibal, Constantine, and Dollhouse
among them. Despite featuring public domain

00:00:56.769 --> 00:01:01.469
characters like Dracula, Dr. Jekyll, Frankenstein’s
monster, and Dorian Gray, the price of bringing

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:04.580
this many monsters to the screen couldn’t
have been cheap.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.560
Vanessa Ives’ departure

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.450
Despite all the interesting characters she's
met over the past three years, Penny Dreadful

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.939
is a tale about Vanessa Ives. The series ended
with her finally finding peace, and while

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:18.740
we’ll never see her tangle with The Creature
or Dorian Grey again, this sudden ending is

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.820
how it was planned.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:26.220
"I see...our lord."

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.049
Showtime CEO David Nevin said to Entertainment
Weekly,

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:35.240
"I always knew it wasn't going to be a really
long-running show—John Logan made that clear

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:35.939
coming in."

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:39.250
While there are plenty of tales you could
tell without her in this dark world, Ives

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:43.430
was the focal point of this show, and we couldn't
imagine it continuing without her. Remember

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:47.170
how The X-Files felt without Mulder? Gross.

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.859
More monsters

00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:52.500
Without Vanessa Ives, Penny Dreadful is pretty
much just a bunch of 19th century ghouls.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.450
If that’s your thing, you'll be seeing a
lot more of them soon. Universal Pictures

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:00.700
is launching its own set of films featuring
the most classic of movie monsters. The series

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:05.890
began with Dracula Untold in 2014. Meanwhile,
The Mummy reboot, starring Tom Cruise, is

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:10.700
scheduled for 2017. Don't be surprised if
TV executives try bringing Frank, Drac, and

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:15.620
the whole monster squad back to capitalize
on Hollywood digging them up from their graves.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.440
It was foretold

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.970
There are various reasons why Penny Dreadful
was canceled, but we're gonna have to go with

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:25.190
show creator John Logan's explanation. Apparently,
he knew this was how the series would end

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:29.350
from the very beginning. But the cast found
out halfway through filming season two. In

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:30.550
Logan’s own words:

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:35.310
"Penny Dreadful was always intended to go
for three years exactly. So, I think we've

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:40.070
told our story well, and thank you for all
your support and hanging in there with us."

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:44.750
All good things come to an end. Sorry, Game
of Thrones fans. You too will know this sting.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.340
We're sure you'll see most of these characters
in other forms soon enough, though.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.380
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:54.400
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know what you’ll miss the most about

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.000
Penny Dreadful...

